[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3411993094","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3411993094","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3411993094,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LXuIG","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T17:32:11Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T17:32:11Z","body":"Are you reusing the parameters of Godot Engine's HLOD?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3411993094/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412017608","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3412017608","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3412017608,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LX0HI","user":{"login":"Saul2022","id":97898580,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdXQVA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97898580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022","html_url":"https://github.com/Saul2022","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T17:36:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T17:36:49Z","body":"Great looking though a bit confused about what skip frames mean.  Like for example an animation is 60 frames, so in level 1 it turna into  55 if you skip frames, then level to you skip 20 frames so now the animation is 40 \r\nFps  at that distance. In that case would it be  easier for people to understand if  instad of skip frames it says current frames or fps? Also for other pr  it would be nice to have  an optional  parameter in the fps lod levels,   where you can  add a vertex animated target, or a option to bake it. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412017608/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412967162","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3412967162","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3412967162,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Lbb76","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T21:44:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T21:46:31Z","body":"Can you upload the testing project somewhere? I'd like to do some benchmarking.\r\n\r\n> This isn't 100% ready yet. I can't hide the Target and Levels parameters right now. \r\n\r\nThis is implemented using `_validate_property()` in each class (and calling `notify_property_list_changed()` at the end of setters that impact property visibility). Check https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/20430236e749306e1968656ffdc7f78e502a0ccc/scene/3d/light_3d.cpp#L324 for an example implementation.\r\n\r\nAlso, you can edit `editor_property_name_processor.cpp` to add capitalizations for `\"fps\"` and `\"lod\"`, so that they appear uppercase in the inspector.\r\n\r\n> Great looking though a bit confused about what skip frames mean. Like for example an animation is 60 frames, so in level 1 it turna into 55 if you skip frames, then level to you skip 20 frames so now the animation is 40\r\n\r\n**Skip Frames** is meant to be understood as \"starting from this distance, update this animation every N + 1 frames\". For example, if set to 2, the animation is updated on every third frame (20 FPS, if the game runs at 60 FPS).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412967162/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3413263042","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3413263042","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3413263042,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LckLC","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T23:49:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T21:54:48Z","body":"> This is implemented using `_validate_property()` in each class (and calling `notify_property_list_changed()` at the end of setters that impact property visibility).\r\n\r\nYes, I tried, but `_validate_property()` doesn't seem to work in `AnimationMixer`, I tried checking it at the beginn