ttps://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3421594351/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536241159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3536241159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3536241159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SxsIH","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T09:17:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T12:21:16Z","body":"~~I think we could combine this now for testing~~. I've added documentation, and everything is working now.\r\nAs @fire mentioned, we should further add Godot's built-in HLOD, which would replace the distance calculation method currently used in this PR, but I think we could add this in a future PR, as it's not as critical right now.\r\n\r\n[EDIT] What could be the CI error?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536241159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536932653","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3536932653","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3536932653,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S0U8t","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T21:42:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T21:42:55Z","body":"1. documentation changed parameters\r\n2. I think you might have a wrong object cast","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536932653/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3557424618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3557424618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3557424618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UCf3q","user":{"login":"InitialCon","id":66960524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2OTYwNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66960524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon","html_url":"https://github.com/InitialCon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/InitialCon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T11:14:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T11:14:43Z","body":"> I've improved the synchronization and revealed useful methods.\r\n\r\nNot sure if this is what you were referring to but it seems as if every skeleton for a given lod is updating simultaneously.\r\nWhen running the testing project performance is at around 7-8ms without FPSLOD enabled and drops down to 4ms with it enabled. However, when a group of skeletons update there is a stutter, with the frametime returning to 7-8ms for one frame. It does not seem like skeleton updates are being spread out currently. Is that something that should be left to the user or done in a follow up pr since even with the stutters the net performance is always better than with FPSLOD disabled?\r\nHere's a picture for reference:\r\n<img width=\"1374\" height=\"662\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251120_130041\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6fe4d1d8-2fd7-409c-b28d-81da19841bf6\" />\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3557424618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566737215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3566737215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3566737215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmBc_","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:02:22Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:02:22Z","body":"Currently, FPSLOD tries to update frames at the same time to synchronize a group of skeletons. Therefore, there are regular delays. This is intentional, as I didn't want it to affect the animation itself. For example, if we have two skeletons that use animations to interact with each other, such as a fight, without synchronization during the FPSLODLevel change, one skeleton's animation might not match the other skeleton's without synchronization.\r\n\r\nHowever, it would also be logical not to use synchronization, as this would update the skeletons' animations at different times rather than in batches, which could reduce latency. However, this would result in animation desynchronization, as I described above. I would like to get the team's recommendation on this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566737215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3606427371","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-3606427371","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":3606427371,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7W9bbr","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-03T11:33:06Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T11:33:06Z","body":"I'd really like to get this into 4.6, at least as an experimental one, but I can't seem to solve the CI issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3606427371/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366276196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-4366276196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":4366276196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBEAWZA","user":{"login":"ashleyseric","id":12580010,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTgwMDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12580010?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric","html_url":"https://github.com/ashleyseric","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleyseric/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-03T13:26:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-03T18:22:40Z","body":"I ran into some errors when I tried to build the editor after merging on Debian 13.  However, I was able to get a build working after adding:\r\n\r\n`#include \"scene/3d/node_3d.h\"` to `animation_mixer.h`  (fixed error `Unknown type name 'Node3D'` on line: `148`)\r\n`#include \"core/object/class_db.h\"` to `fpslod_level.h`  (fixed error `Incomplete type 'ClassDB' named in nested name specifier` on lines: `43` to `49`)\r\n\r\nPerhaps this is the same issue that's causing the Linux CI to fail?  Everything works except I am experiencing editor crashes when trying to create/select/assign an `fps_lod_level` resource, though I may be messing something up in the process of building the editor with .NET support (my c++ skills are a bit rusty).\r\n\r\nRegarding synchronisation, I strongly feel that there should be some logic to spread the processing out into as few AnimationMixers being updated on any given frame as possible while still respecting their `skip_frames` values.  To me, spreading the load across frames is the primary reason to want a feature like this and forcing frame spikes to sync every mixer on the same frame negates it's value across most use-cases I can think of.\r\n\r\nTo solve the issue of syncing skeletons that are interacting with each other I would propose adding something along the lines of an `fps_sync_index` int on the AnimationMixer that defaults to `-1` and developers can set those where necessary.  The system could then align the update intervals for any AnimationMixers that share the same `fps_sync_index` value that isn't `-1` and process them in sync while allowing all others to remain automatically offset to spread the load across as many frames as possible.  For example:  If 2 character start fighting each other, I could assign them `fps_sync_index = 1`. If 2 other characters interact with each other in another area of the map, I could then assign them `fps_sync_index = 2`.  Both of those character interactions would then be synced, but the two separate `fps_sync_index` groups could be processed in offset frames from each other, essentially halving the per-frame load (unless their `skip_frames` values are `0`).\r\n\r\nCorrect me if I'm wrong but as far as I can tell from reading through the code changes, there currently doesn't appear to be any mechanism to intentionally sync mixers, but rather it happens to align the update intervals of any that are first activated on the same frame since they each track their own frame counters independently and only increment them while they're active.  So if you currently spawned 2 identical mixers with a `skip_frames` values of `5` but deactivated one, waited a frame and then activated it again, they would no longer be in sync with each other.  You could reference `Engine::get_singleton()->get_process_frames()` / `get_physics_frames()` for syncing rather than independent frame counters but that wouldn't solve the issue of spreading the load for mixers that don't need to be sync'd.\r\n\r\nPerhaps there could be a static list of all mixers with `fps_lod` enabled.  The mixers could add/remove themselves from that list as they're activated/deactived.  When a mixer is set active, it could look at the `frame_offset` and `fps_sync_index` of each mixer in the list and assign it's `frame_offset` based on what would spread the load as evenly as possible across frames.  A mixer might also need to adjust it's own `frame_offset` value when it's `skip_frames` or `fps_sync_index` values are changed to maintain an even spread.  I'm not very familiar with Godot's source code so there may be a simpler approach, this is just conceptually what came to mind when I was looking through the code diffs.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366276196/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366618280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-4366618280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":4366618280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBEVOqA","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-03T16:22:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-03T16:22:16Z","body":"A static list of all mixers, so a godot engine autoload or singleton? That doesn't seem like it is very generalized. Thoughts?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366618280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5848133528","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-5848133528","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":5848133528,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXJNvmA","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-26T17:01:55Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T17:02:53Z","body":"I performed a rebase to continue working on this.\r\nThe CI is throwing errors; I’d really appreciate it if someone could point out the cause.\r\n\r\nHas something changed with `D_METHOD`? Almost all the errors point to this method.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5848133528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5848630876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111730#issuecomment-5848630876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111730","id":5848630876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXJsGXA","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-26T18:12:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T18:12:10Z","body":"According to the logs, the file doesn't have the full definition of `ClassDB`, so you will need to add an include with its header path.\r\n\r\nAlso, is there anywhere in the engine where the binding is defined in the header?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5848630876/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]